<meta type=article>
  <title | Inline TeX Shortcuts — End-to-End Fixture>
  <author | Test Suite>
</meta>

<section | Ordinals in prose>
The 1^{st} edition appeared in 1984. The 2^{nd} printing followed in 1985,
and the 3^{rd} expanded edition arrived in 1990.

<section | Chemistry in prose>
Water is H_{2}O. Carbon dioxide is CO_{2}. Sulfuric acid is H_{2}SO_{4}.

<section | Nested shortcuts in prose>
The variable x^{y_{1}} demonstrates nested super- and subscript in flowing text.

<section | Shortcuts inside named tags>
<aside | The 1^{st} law of thermodynamics: energy H_{2}O is conserved.>

<section | Mixed prose and tag usage>
In the body, iron-56 can be written ^{56}Fe. Inside a tag: <aside | the isotope ^{56}Fe is stable>.

<section | Sigil at a paragraph boundary in a tag body>
<aside | The mass-energy relation is written E=mc^{2}

^{56}Fe is the most stable isotope, so a sigil may open a paragraph too.>
